So, now what we have made this structural change and really structured the IR interface, here is what I want to do. Instead of having pyton source code for Modules* under `src/pycsl`, I want to move existing *.py files under two directories:
- `src/pycsl/frontend/python` for roughly Module 1/2 (every thing before the IR)
- `src/pycsl/backend/` for all Module 4-6 python code (including directories `module5/` and `module6_whyml/` to move under `src/pycsl/backend/`)
I do not know where module 3 should be.

The idea is to use this structure later for other languages:
- `src/pycsl/frontend/c` for C code
- `src/pycsl/frontend/go` for Go code
- `src/pycsl/frontend/rust` for Rust code

Provide your feedback on these changes and future evolutions by writing the specification `structuring.py`.

